.TH SYSMON 1 "November 2026" "sysmon 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sysmon \- graphical system monitor for Raspberry Pi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sysmon
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sysmon
shows live rolling charts of CPU utilization, disk I/O, network I/O,
CPU and drive temperatures, and fan speed, updating every second with
60 seconds of history. It requires a graphical desktop session.
.PP
Drive temperatures are read with
.BR "sudo smartctl" ,
so the user must be able to run
.B smartctl
through
.B sudo
without a password.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sysmon.ini
Optional configuration file for hiding drives and network interfaces,
setting a case fan tachometer GPIO pin, and passing extra
.B smartctl
options. An annotated example is installed at
.IR /usr/share/doc/sysmon/examples/sysmon.ini .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/sysmon/venv
Python virtual environment the application runs in, created when the
package is configured.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartctl (8)
